+## Self-hosting
+
+Fizzy can be deployed as a single container on a Linux server with Docker. The
+container runs the web server and Solid Queue background workers together.
+SQLite databases (including the job and cache databases) and uploaded files are
+stored in the `fizzy-storage` Docker volume, so they survive app rebuilds and
+deploys. Kamal Proxy obtains and renews the HTTPS certificate for you.
+
+1. Point a DNS record for your public app hostname at the server. Make sure the
+   server is reachable over SSH by a user with Docker access, and ports 80
+   and 443 are open.
+2. Edit `config/deploy.yml`: set the server SSH hostname, public app hostname
+   (`proxy.host` and `FIZZY_HOST`), SMTP server and sender settings, and your
+   GitHub username/image path. The builder defaults to amd64; set
+   `builder.arch` to `arm64` for an ARM server. Create a GitHub token with
+   read and write access to GitHub Packages.
+3. Copy `.kamal/secrets.example` to `.kamal/secrets` and replace the values.
+   Set `SECRET_KEY_BASE` to a generated secret (`bin/rails secret`); keep it
+   unchanged between deploys. Set `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` to your Rails master key
+   (or generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32` if you do not have one).
+4. Run `bin/kamal setup` from the repository checkout. Later releases can be
+   deployed with `bin/kamal deploy`.
+
+The server hostname is the SSH target and can differ from the public app
+hostname. Keep `.kamal/secrets` private; it is ignored by git. Back up the
+server's `fizzy-storage` Docker volume regularly, since it contains both the
+SQLite databases and uploaded files.
diff --git a/config/deploy.yml b/config/deploy.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..389fd24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/deploy.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+service: fizzy
+image: your-github-username/fizzy
+
+builder:
+  arch: amd64
+
+servers:
+  web:
+    hosts:
+      - your-server.example.com
+
+proxy:
+  ssl: true
+  host: fizzy.example.com
+
+registry:
+  server: ghcr.io
+  username: your-github-username
+  password:
+    - KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
+
+# Persist primary, cache, queue, cable, and Active Storage data across releases.
+volumes:
+  - fizzy-storage:/rails/storage
+
+env:
+  clear:
+    RAILS_ENV: production
+    FIZZY_HOST: fizzy.example.com
+    SMTP_ADDRESS: smtp.example.com
+    SMTP_PORT: 587
+    SMTP_DOMAIN: example.com
+    SMTP_STARTTLS: true
+    MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS: "Fizzy <noreply@fizzy.example.com>"
+    WEB_CONCURRENCY: 1
+    JOB_CONCURRENCY: 1
+  secret:
+    - RAILS_MASTER_KEY
+    - SECRET_KEY_BASE
+    - SMTP_USERNAME
+    - SMTP_PASSWORD
